==Trivia==
*In [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese version]], this stage takes place in '''Nagasaki Prefecture'''. In the Taiwanese version, stage 1 is set in '''Taiwan''' and Korea appears later as [[Philippines (Empire of Cats)|stage 6]].
*Korea's base is [[wikipedia:Gwanghwamun|Gwanghwamun]], the fourth and largest gate of [[wikipedia:Gyeongbokgung|Gyeongbokgung Palace]] in Seoul.
*Taiwan's base is [[wikipedia:Taipei 101|Taipei 101]], a 101-story skyscraper that is the tallest building in Taiwan.
*[[Earth (Cats of the Cosmos)|Earth]] reuses Nagasaki Prefecture's enemy base.
*In the [[The Battle Cats|English]], Korean and Taiwanese versions, this stage's enemy base in Chapter 1 changes after the first clear. Initially, it uses the gray castle tower from Nagasaki Prefecture and Earth. In subsequent [[Battle|battles]], the base changes to Gwanghwamun (BCEN/BCKR) or Taipei 101 (BCTW).
*The player is guaranteed to get a Superior [[Treasure]] when completing the stage in Chapter 1.
**This is not true for the [[The Battle Cats Unite!|Nintendo Switch]] port of the game.
*[[Doge]] and [[Ms. Sign]] are technically both introduced here, making Korea/Nagasaki and [[Brazil (Empire of Cats)|Brazil/Tochigi]] the only [[Empire of Cats]] stages besides [[Zombie Outbreaks]] to introduce multiple new enemies in a single chapter.
*Prior to [[Version 11.7 Update|version 11.7]], there were 8 extra Doges which spawned after bringing the enemy base down to 50% HP, with a delay of 1 second between each Doge.
*In The Battle Cats Unite!, when playing the Korea stage for the first time, it uses the Japanese sprite instead. However, it swaps back to the international sprite once replaying the stage.

